<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Amyloid Plaque Deposition">
  <data key="d0">intermediate</data>
  <data key="d1">Accumulation of amyloid-beta peptides forming plaques in the brain, a hallmark of Alzheimer's disease pathology.</data>
</node>
<node id="Tau Pathology and Neurodegeneration">
  <data key="d0">intermediate</data>
  <data key="d1">Abnormal tau protein phosphorylation leading to neurofibrillary tangles and neuronal loss.</data>
</node>
<node id="Cognitive Decline and Memory Impairment">
  <data key="d0">intermediate</data>
  <data key="d1">Progressive impairment in memory, executive function, and other cognitive domains characteristic of Alzheimer's disease.</data>
</node>
<node id="Neuropsychiatric Symptoms">
  <data key="d0">intermediate</data>
  <data key="d1">Behavioral and psychiatric symptoms such as depression, agitation, and hallucinations associated with Alzheimer's disease.</data>
</node>
<node id="Brain Atrophy and Structural Changes">
  <data key="d0">intermediate</data>
  <data key="d1">Loss of brain volume and structural changes including hippocampal and ventricular atrophy detected by MRI.</data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Hypometabolism and Functional Brain Changes">
  <data key="d0">intermediate</data>
  <data key="d1">Reduced brain glucose metabolism and functional impairments detected by FDG-PET imaging.</data>
</node>
<node id="Demographic and Vascular Risk Factors">
